  "bloques": [
    {
      "tipo": "explicacion",
      "titulo": {
        "en": "Talking about sport"
      },
      "texto": {
        "en": "With ball sports, use **jugar al**: **jugar al fútbol**, **al baloncesto** or **al tenis**. Common collocations include **hacer natación**, **hacer atletismo**, **hacer ciclismo** and **hacer yoga**. **Practicar** also works with many sports: **practico natación**, **practico yoga**. These are common patterns, not a rule that depends on whether a sport uses a ball.\n\nTo report a result, use **ganar**, **perder** or **empatar**. Scores are commonly read with **a**: **Ganaron dos a uno; empataron a cero**. **¿Cómo quedaron?** asks for the result. You can say **ganar a** a person or team: **El Sevilla ganó al Betis**. **Perder contra** a team is also common.\n\nPeople include **el jugador**, **el entrenador**, **el árbitro** and **los aficionados**. Sports venues include **el campo** de fútbol, **la pista** de tenis, **la piscina** and **el estadio**.\n\n**Ser de** a team means to support it: **Soy del** Athletic. **Ser aficionado/a a** means to be a fan of something: **Soy aficionada al** ciclismo."
      }
    },
